 "final_summary": "The bug was caused by case-sensitive boolean parsing in `parse_bool`. The fix added case-insensitive checks by converting input strings to lowercase before comparison, ensuring 'TRUE', 'true', 'TrUe', etc. are all recognized as True. This makes boolean queries case-insensitive as required.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/convert.py b/tracker/convert.py\nindex db3b63f..83cedea 100644\n--- a/tracker/convert.py\n+++ b/tracker/convert.py\n@@ -30,9 +30,9 @@ def parse_bool(value, default=None, name=\"value\"):\n     if isinstance(value, bool):\n         return value\n     text = str(value).strip()\n-    if text in TRUE_VALUES:\n+    if text in TRUE_VALUES or text.lower() in TRUE_VALUES:\n         return True\n-    if text in FALSE_VALUES:\n+    if text in FALSE_VALUES or text.lower() in FALSE_VALUES:\n         return False\n     raise ValidationError(f\"{name} must be a boolean\", {name: \"not_a_boolean\"})\n \n",
